Welcome to Episode 1 of Franklin, a series in which I build a city.

In this episode we cover Prehistory, in this case before 1638 or so. We're gonna talk about geology, hydrology, and Lenape culture. 

Note to copyright guys: the music is a public domain recording of Edvard Greig's "Anitra's Dance" from Musopen -- I did not steal your music. You can see for yourself here: https://musopen.org/music/777-peer-gynt-suite-no-1-op-46/

And the title music is a recording of Mussorgsky's "Night on a Bald Mountain", conducted by Leopold Stokowski with the Philadelphia Orchestra in 1940. I believe it is well out of copyright. http://publicdomain.lafauniere.info/index.php?-table=media&-search=Leopold+Stokowski&-action=browse&-submit=Submit&-cursor=159&-skip=150&-limit=30&-mode=list&-recordid=media%3Fpk_media%3D6441

